# Backend

Python decides. Solidity enforces. Do not reject trades only in FastAPI.

Services: credit engine, risk engine, policy generator, Monad indexer/client.

Proposed API: `GET /api/credit/{wallet}`, `/api/risk/{wallet}`, `/api/policy/{wallet}`, `/api/trades/{wallet}`, `/api/positions/{wallet}`, `/api/markets`. Writes: `POST /credit/evaluate`, `/risk/evaluate`, `/policy/propose`.

Postgres holds historical state (users, wallets, trades, positions, markets, credit_profiles, credit_scores, risk_scores, risk_events, credit_accounts, credit_vaults, risk_policies, policy_history). Monad holds verifiable execution.

Score and adaptive formulas live in `docs/credit-model.md` and `docs/risk-model.md`. Keep them deterministic.
